  "factor_name": "Market-Residualized Volatility-Normalized 20-Day Momentum",
  "version": "1.0",
  "calculation": {
    "expression": "rank_cs( (log(close/close[-20]) - beta_60 * mean_cs(log(close/log(close[-20]))) ) / (std_30(daily_log_return)*sqrt(30)) ); signal=rolling_mean(rank_cs_centered,3)",
    "description": "Compute each asset's 20-day log return residualized against the equal-weight cross-asset market return using a lagged 60-day rolling beta, normalize by 30-day realized volatility, cross-sectionally rank and center, then smooth over three observations. Negative direction is used for portfolio scoring because the validated relationship is contrarian. All inputs are lag-safe."
